HOW TO ATTRIBUTE THIS DATA
--------------------------
A suggested attribution line for schools, curricula, or software that reuse
this inventory:

    "English decoding inventory from the Vocabulary Measurement System
     (github/…), CC BY 4.0. Compiled from published orthographic research;
     see CREDITS.md."


WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS — AND AN IMPORTANT DISTINCTION
------------------------------------------------------
This license applies to THIS PROJECT'S OWN COMPILATION and arrangement of the
data. The underlying FACTS about English orthography (that "sh" spells /ʃ/,
that "c" is soft before e/i/y, that "farm" is a base morpheme, etc.) are not
themselves owned by anyone and are not subject to copyright.

This inventory was compiled independently from the published research findings
credited in CREDITS.md. It does NOT reproduce, and is not a substitute for, any
copyrighted curriculum's specific text, curated word lists, or scope-and-
sequence arrangement. Researchers and programs are credited for their findings
by scholarly citation, which neither copyright nor this license requires — it
is a matter of academic and professional respect.
